-- Normalise stored phone numbers to E.164 ("+34689590123").
--
-- GENERATED 2026-10-18 from the live database by a read-only script that
-- applies the SAME rule as src/utils/phone.ts (libphonenumber-js, default country ES). Plain SQL
-- can't do this: 31 stored numbers carry a national trunk "0" after the country code
-- ("+44 07368…", "+33 06…") that libphonenumber drops and a regex would keep.
--
-- Run AFTER the phone-normalisation code is deployed. That code already writes E.164 and matches
-- either spelling, so it works before and after this file — this just converts the existing data.
--
-- What it does
--   clients    : 1020 rows rewritten
--                 = 984 unique numbers + 36 duplicate clusters given one canonical owner
--   therapists : 4 rows rewritten
--
-- What it deliberately does NOT do
--   * Touch 148 rows that duplicate another client's number (125 clusters). Only one row
--     per number may hold the canonical value under clients_phone_active_unique, so the others
--     keep their current spelling until the duplicate-merge review. Each cluster's canonical
--     owner is the row with the most bookings (then the oldest), i.e. the likely merge survivor.
--     Cluster rows that already hold the canonical value (89 clusters) are left as they are.
--   * Touch soft-deleted rows.
--   * Touch updated_at: this is a format change, not a user edit.
--
-- Safety
--   * Every row is matched on id AND its current value, so a number edited since this file was
--     generated is skipped rather than overwritten. Re-running the file is a no-op.
--   * One statement per table inside one transaction: if anything collides with the unique
--     index (a client created since generation with one of these numbers), the whole file rolls
--     back and nothing changes. In that case, ask for the file to be regenerated.
--   * clients_history logs one UPDATE per row (that table has no actor/timestamp columns, so the
--     sweep isn't attributable there).
--
-- Data only: no schema change, so no `prisma db pull` / `prisma generate` afterwards.


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- STEP 0 — Preview (optional)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SELECT count(*) FILTER (WHERE client_phone !~ '^[+][1-9][0-9]{6,14}$')::int AS not_e164_shaped,
       count(*)::int AS with_phone
FROM clients
WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND client_phone IS NOT NULL AND btrim(client_phone) <> '';


